PHASE 14 — ⭐ Gamification & Point System
Goal

Encourage positive actions and "good Samaritan" behavior by rewarding users with a points-based system.

Step 1 — Database Update

In Supabase, update your existing tables:

Add to Users table:

total_points (integer, default: 0)

Create new points_history table:

id (PK)

user_id (FK → Users.id)

action (string, e.g., "Reported found item", "Item returned to owner")

points_earned (integer)

created_at (timestamp)

Step 2 — Define Point Values

Establish the reward logic in your backend:

Report a legitimate found item = +10 points

Item successfully claimed and returned = +50 points (Awarded to the finder)

Step 3 — Backend API Updates

Modify existing routes:

PUT /api/claims/:id → When an admin approves a claim, trigger a function to add 50 points to the found_item.user_id (the finder) and log it in points_history.

POST /api/found-items → Add 10 points to the reporting user.

Create new route:

GET /api/users/leaderboard → Fetch the top 10 users ranked by total_points in descending order.

Step 4 — Frontend UI

Create:

Profile Badge: Display the user's total_points on their dashboard and profile page.

Leaderboard Page: A public page showing the top point earners on campus to spark friendly competition.

Point Notifications: Add to your Phase 11 notification system (e.g., "You earned 50 points! Your found item was returned.").

Step 5 — Anti-Abuse Rules (Security)

To prevent users from gaming the system:

Admins can view point histories.

If an admin deletes a fake "Found Item" report, deduct the 10 points.

Deliverable

A fully functional point system, transaction history, and campus leaderboard.

